  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: CommAddDisc 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "You attend a monthly \u201Cresearch open house\u201D where a lab team
    shares their new ideas and early lab experiments with the community. They describe
    several new drug compounds being tested in the lab and invite feedback on which
    kinds of treatments would be most meaningful to cancer patients. When meeting
    with the team, you advocate for affordable treatment options that prioritize
    the patients\u2019 quality of life, both short- and long-term.\n\nIn this situation,
    what role does a community advocate play in the Discovery stage?"
  explanation: "By sharing the patient perspective, community advocates help researchers
    focus on what matters most to patients and the community. This guidance can shape
    research priorities before preclinical studies begin. By speaking up about patients\u2019
    needs and experiences, advocates help ensure early research addresses real-world
    concerns and has meaningful impact for the people it aims to help."
  correctAnswer: 'D: Helping researchers understand patient priorities early on'
  incorrectAnswer1: 'A: Designing and conducting lab experiments on cancer cells'
  incorrectAnswer2: 'B: Approving or denying specific drug compounds for clinical
    trials'
  incorrectAnswer3: "C: Organizing the research team\u2019s data and tracking patient
    samples"
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
